# node_modules/, .env, and OS/editor files are already covered by the
# root .gitignore (patterns there apply recursively). This file only adds
# what's specific to the backend: the local SQLite database file it
# creates on first run at the path configured by DB_PATH (see .env.example).
# The seed data files that ship WITH the project (server/data/*.json) are
# not touched by this pattern and remain committed.
data/*.sqlite3
data/*.sqlite3-journal
data/*.sqlite3-shm
data/*.sqlite3-wal
